.TH ALARM 2 "March 2026" "Substrate" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
alarm \- schedule delivery of SIGALRM
.SH LIBRARY
Substrate libc
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <unistd.h>

unsigned int alarm(unsigned int seconds);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR alarm ()
arms or cancels the calling process's real-time interval timer.
A nonzero
.I seconds
value schedules delivery of
.B SIGALRM
after approximately that many seconds of wall-clock time.
A zero value cancels any pending real-time timer.
.P
Substrate implements
.BR alarm ()
as a compatibility alias for
.BR setitimer (2)
with
.BR ITIMER_REAL .
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success,
.BR alarm ()
returns the number of seconds remaining on the previously scheduled alarm.
If a prior alarm had a fractional second remaining, the return value is rounded up to the next whole second.
.SH ERRORS
.BR alarm ()
does not report errors separately; a failure to arm the underlying timer returns 0.
.SH NOTES
Only one
.B ITIMER_REAL
timer exists per process.
Calling
.BR alarm ()
replaces any earlier
.BR alarm ()
or
.BR setitimer ()
configuration for
.BR ITIMER_REAL .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getitimer (2),
.BR setitimer (2),
.BR signal (2)
